# Constant field extension of a separably generated function field

Theorem statement:
`AlgebraicCurve.
exists_finiteDimensional_isSeparable_adjoin_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed`
(`3a95c22c-d63d-58cf-8425-27387f799760`), by Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `f712fcd4-03e1-57d7-b600-a62920b8a436`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let $K, F, K', F'$ be fields with algebra structures $K \to F$, $K' \to F'$, $K \to K'$, $F \to F'$
and $K \to F'$, the last compatible with the towers $K \to K' \to F'$ and $K \to F \to F'$, and
suppose $K$ is algebraically closed. Assume: (i) there is $x \in F$ transcendental over $K$ such
that $F$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field $K(x) \subseteq F$ generated by $x$; (ii)
there is $x \in F'$ transcendental over $K'$ such that $F'$ is finite-dimensional over $K'(x)
\subseteq F'$; (iii) the intermediate field of $F'/K'$ generated over $K'$ by the image of $F$ under
$F \to F'$ is all of $F'$. Then there exists $t' \in F'$ such that $F'$ is finite-dimensional over
the intermediate field $K'(t') \subseteq F'$ and $F'$ is separable over $K'(t')$.

This is the statement that a constant field extension $F' = K' \cdot F$ of a one-variable function
field over an algebraically closed constant field is again separably generated, the witness being
the image of a separating transcendental downstairs. It is used in the construction of places of
$F'$ restricting to a prescribed place of $F$
([`AlgebraicCurve.Place.exists_comap_algebraMap_eq_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed`]
(thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Place.
exists_comap_algebraMap_eq_of_constantFieldExtension_of_isAlgClosed)).

